      "feedback": "Prior h1 is supported but incomplete: the measured enantiomer gaps were 6.40 and 8.18 mL, while both members of each pair were overpredicted. Thus stereochemical differences and shared scaffold bias coexist. Prior h2's broad substitution sensitivity remains plausible, but the fluoro response of 27.45 mL, versus 58.5 mL for the methoxy member under different conditions, weakens transfer of the exceptional value across the scaffold. Prior h3 gained a third high-retention fused-alcohol observation at 37.85 mL with signed error -7.21, but substitution and condition contributions remain unresolved. Prior h4 identified a numerical problem: the boron response was 5.90 mL versus a 0.53 mL frozen center; nevertheless, its response was relatively low, so this does not establish universal underprediction of boron compounds. Prior h5 does not support a common error direction: the selected beta-hydroxy ester, alpha-hydroxy ester and hydroxy ketone had signed errors -6.19, +12.54 and -4.22 mL. Connectivity, stereochemistry and conditions need more controlled comparisons. The piperazinone and two sulfonyl cyclic observations additionally revealed substantial underprediction. These are frozen premeasurement errors, not errors of the retrained model; initial observations carry no such errors."
